---

Log in so Nx Cloud knows you're a member of the workspace and gives you the
[access set for logged-in members](#permissions).
CI runs use [CI access tokens](/docs/kb/access-tokens) instead.

{% aside type="caution" title="Workspaces that use `nxCloudAccessToken`" %}
`nx login` doesn't run while `nx.json` has `nxCloudAccessToken`.
Run [`npx nx-cloud convert-to-nx-cloud-id`](/docs/reference/nx-cloud-cli#nx-cloud-convert-to-nx-cloud-id)
first to switch the workspace to `nxCloudId`.
{% /aside %}

## Log in

1. Run `npx nx login` from your workspace.
   It shows a code and opens Nx Cloud in your browser.
1. On the **Nx Cloud CLI login** page, check that the code matches the one in your terminal and
   select **Approve**.

![The Nx Cloud CLI login page showing a code to compare with the terminal, with Approve and Deny buttons](../../../assets/nx-cloud/cli-login-approval.avif)

If no browser opens, open the URL the terminal printed.

<!-- TODO: Remove this aside once few developers still log in with a personal access token. -->

{% aside type="caution" title="Already logged in with a personal access token" %}
When this machine is logged in to the Nx Cloud instance with a personal access token, `nx login`
asks you to run `npx nx logout` first.
That logs you out and revokes the stored token.
Then run `npx nx login` again.
{% /aside %}

## Check your login

```shell
npx nx login --status
```

The command shows the account you're logged in as.

## CLI sessions

In Nx Cloud, open **Personal settings** from the account menu and select **Access tokens**.
The **CLI sessions** card lists each login.

![The CLI sessions card listing one signed-in device, with Sign out and Sign out of all CLI sessions](../../../assets/nx-cloud/cli-sessions.avif)

**Sign out** ends one session, and **Sign out of all CLI sessions** ends every one.
A device you sign out needs `nx login` again.

## Log out

```shell
npx nx logout
```

With logins for several Nx Cloud instances, see
[`nx-cloud logout`](/docs/reference/nx-cloud-cli#nx-cloud-logout).

## Permissions

Set both access levels in your workspace's
[access control settings](https://cloud.nx.app/go/workspace/settings/access).

### Workspace ID access level

The **Default access level** setting covers anyone who isn't logged in, or isn't a member of the
workspace's Nx Cloud organization.
It starts at `read-write`.
Lower it to `read-only` or `none` for any repository that people outside your team can see, such as
an open source repository or one that's visible across your organization but only editable by one team.

### Personal access token access level

The **Logged in users** setting covers workspace members who ran `nx login`.
Set it to `read-only`, `read-write`, or `no-cache`.

## Personal access tokens (PATs)

Use a personal access token only where you can't log in: scripts that call the Public API without
the Nx Cloud CLI, and CI jobs that
[publish conformance rules](/docs/reference/nx-cloud-cli#nx-cloud-configure).
Other CI steps use a CI access token.
Create a personal access token under **Personal settings** > **Access tokens**.
